    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n91256" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτύρομαι</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῡ]</span>, aor. 2
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπτύρην [ῠ</span>] <i><span class="en">
			Plu.
			<u>Fab.</u>
			3
		</span></i>, inf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτυρῆναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ax.</u>
					370a
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be scared</i> or <i>frightened</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Mul.</u>
				1.25
			</span></i>; of the soul, <i><span class="en">
				M.Ant.
				8.45
			</span></i>; esp. of horses, <i>shy, start</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				2.19
			</span></i>, Plu.l.c.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span>
			<i>at</i> a thing, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Marc.</u>
				6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φωνῇ π. ὥσπερ θηρίον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					2.800c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
				</span></i>
			 Bybl. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Eus.
				<u>PE</u>
				1.10
			</span></i>: c. acc., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τὸν θάνατον</span>
			<i>start at, be alarmed at</i> death, Pl.l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔν τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ep.Phil.</u>
					1.28
				</span></i>
			.</div>
